{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 33}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2020-12-20T04:28:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 266620, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/266620/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-06-18T03:28:06Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2020-12-20T04:28:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 266700, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/266700/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-06-19T13:39:29Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n   Privacy and security properties not provided by PSKs are also\n   included.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-05-06T21:17:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 274715, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/274715/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-11-02T22:17:49Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n   Privacy and security properties not provided by PSKs are also\n   included.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-05-06T21:17:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 277525, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/277525/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/41/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-12-10T03:05:16Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n   Privacy and security properties not provided by PSKs are also\n   included.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-05-06T21:17:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279126, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279126/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/41/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-21T20:00:33Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n   Privacy and security properties not provided by PSKs are also\n   included.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-05-06T21:17:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279127, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279127/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/41/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-21T20:01:39Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in TLS.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs\n   under certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases, provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support\n   in the context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for\n   applications in various use cases to help meet these assumptions.\n   Privacy and security properties not provided by PSKs are also\n   included.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-05-06T21:17:49Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279130, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279130/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wg/"], "time": "2021-01-21T20:12:21Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3 as defined in\n   RFC 8446.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  It discusses PSK use cases,\n   provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support in the\n   context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for applications in\n   various use cases to help meet these assumptions.  It also lists the\n   privacy and security properties that are not provided by TLS when\n   external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-08-24T20:19:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 280847, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/280847/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wg/"], "time": "2021-02-20T21:19:23Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3 as defined in\n   RFC 8446.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  It discusses PSK use cases,\n   provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support in the\n   context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for applications in\n   various use cases to help meet these assumptions.  It also lists the\n   privacy and security properties that are not provided by TLS when\n   external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-08-24T20:19:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 281390, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/281390/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/43/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-02-24T21:24:59Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3 as defined in\n   RFC 8446.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  It discusses PSK use cases,\n   provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support in the\n   context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for applications in\n   various use cases to help meet these assumptions.  It also lists the\n   privacy and security properties that are not provided by TLS when\n   external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-08-24T20:19:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 281525, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/281525/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/16/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-02-27T02:37:58Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3 as defined in\n   RFC 8446.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  It discusses PSK use cases,\n   provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support in the\n   context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for applications in\n   various use cases to help meet these assumptions.  It also lists the\n   privacy and security properties that are not provided by TLS when\n   external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-08-24T20:19:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 291643, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/291643/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-08-05T22:40:38Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3 as defined in\n   RFC 8446.  It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions and demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  It discusses PSK use cases,\n   provisioning processes, and TLS stack implementation support in the\n   context of these assumptions.  It provides advice for applications in\n   various use cases to help meet these assumptions.  It also lists the\n   privacy and security properties that are not provided by TLS when\n   external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2021-08-24T20:19:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 292187, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/292187/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2021-08-20T19:50:17Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-04-16T17:28:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 294501, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/294501/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2021-10-13T17:28:24Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-04-16T17:28:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 295602, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/295602/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/14/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-10-29T01:04:05Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-04-16T17:28:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 295640, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/295640/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/111/", "/api/v1/doc/state/15/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-10-29T16:16:39Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-04-16T17:28:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 297506, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/297506/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/15/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-11-12T04:28:03Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-04-16T17:28:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 297940, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/297940/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-11-19T08:35:48Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-04-16T17:28:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 298623, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/298623/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2021-12-07T23:08:39Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-06-12T12:49:40Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 298686, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/298686/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2021-12-09T13:49:40Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-06-12T12:49:40Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 298718, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/298718/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-12-09T22:17:38Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-06-12T12:49:40Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 298735, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/298735/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-12-10T04:03:58Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   This document lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under\n   certain assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  This document discusses PSK use cases\n   and provisioning processes.  This document provides advice for\n   applications to help meet these assumptions.  This document also\n   lists the privacy and security properties that are not provided by\n   TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-06-12T12:49:40Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 298972, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/298972/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2021-12-16T15:28:46Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  It also discusses PSK use cases and\n   provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security\n   properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are\n   used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-07-15T13:55:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 299681, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/299681/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2022-01-11T14:55:14Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  It also discusses PSK use cases and\n   provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security\n   properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are\n   used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-07-15T13:55:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 300928, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/300928/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2022-02-03T22:33:06Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  It also discusses PSK use cases and\n   provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security\n   properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are\n   used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-07-15T13:55:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 300929, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/300929/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2022-02-03T22:36:17Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  It also discusses PSK use cases and\n   provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security\n   properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are\n   used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-07-15T13:55:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 300932, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/300932/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2022-02-03T23:46:42Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  It also discusses PSK use cases and\n   provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security\n   properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are\n   used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-07-15T13:55:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 300934, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/300934/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2022-02-03T23:46:42Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  It also discusses PSK use cases and\n   provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the privacy and security\n   properties that are not provided by TLS 1.3 when external PSKs are\n   used.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance/", "expires": "2022-07-15T13:55:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 300968, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-external-psk-guidance", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/300968/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2022-02-04T16:15:24Z", "title": "Guidance for External PSK Usage in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document provides usage guidance for external Pre-Shared Keys\n   (PSKs) in Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.3 as defined in RFC 8446.\n   It lists TLS security properties provided by PSKs under certain\n   assumptions, and then demonstrates how violations of these\n   assumptions lead to attacks.  Advice for applications to help meet\n   these assumptions is provided.  This document also discusses PSK use\n   cases and provisioning processes.  Finally, it lists the priva